+### [Insertion into Spatial Hierarchies](13180-insertion-into-spatial-hierarchies.md)
+Algorithmic process of adding primitives to a hierarchy. It solves the problem of maintaining spatial coherence in dynamic scenes. Unlike static build methods, it processes primitives incrementally, making it suitable for dynamic environments but sensitive to insertion order.
 
 ## Background
-Spatial hierarchies originated in ray tracing to accelerate object intersection tests [S1, unofficial]. Variations include octrees, BSP trees, and KD trees [S1, unofficial]. They are widely used in volume rendering to skip empty space and reduce sampling costs.
+Originating from early ray tracing acceleration techniques, spatial hierarchies such as octrees, BSP trees, and KD trees were developed to optimize point location by recursive search [S1, unofficial]. They are widely used in computer graphics for rendering complex scenes and volumes.
